> IMHO, Nethack has Moria beat cold for variety and complexity. I've found
> Nethack much harder than Moria. On the other hand, Moria's spell system
> is far superior to Nethack's; Wizards and Priests in Moria actually
> become quite powerful at high levels.

IMO both games have features which make them worth playing (that's why I
play both :-) Moria has those nice large dungeons, the shopkeepers, some of
whom have their name for keeping you out of their shop, and then there are
those louses and flies, which can make your life quite hard once you're
stuck in the middle of a room full with them... What concerns the complex-
ity, especially of the monster types, nethack wins hands down. The moria
monsters are not really intelligent... But some things about wearing items
are better with moria, for example, you can have a two-handed weapon and a
shield at the same time, as you wear the shield on your arm, not in one
hand.
  Anyway, you can have challenging games with both of them. In moria, I
currently have a level 18 dwarf, who beats his foes up with a two-handed
sword...
  What I would like to see is a game with the best of both worlds...
                          That'd be really WOW!
